# Allocations LeakSanitizer reaches through this tree but which this
# tree does not own.
#
# The font configuration library builds a process-wide cache the first
# time a font is asked for and holds it until the process ends, by its
# own design; the XML parser it reads its configuration files with is
# reached only from there. Neither allocation belongs to a context, so
# neither is freed when one ends, and neither grows with the work a
# process does -- a job server serving a million pages holds the same
# cache it held after the first. They are named here so that the leaks
# the tree does own can be held to zero.
leak:libfontconfig
leak:libexpat
